From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:00:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/56] Scroll the Markdown preview with the editor in Split
 view

When the editor half scrolls (wheel, keys, cursor moving off screen), the
preview scrolls so the top-level block at the editor's first visible line
sits at the top. One way only: scrolling the preview leaves the editor
alone. Positions are estimated from source lines per block, as the preview
widget does not report block positions. Checked at most every 50 ms after
an input event. View menu "Sync preview scrolling" (config
markdown_sync_scroll, on by default).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

